  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186054676,
      "id": "3123f8ed-a1ca-52b7-8427-2f3b60d9e68a",
      "title": "Identifying Points That Lie on a Line"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1497da22-68c6-5ffd-9b2f-67e39620a8b6",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186054676/assets/b0ccec7a39dbe0524d54ce7c607c38258353ce6bc5294cdbaaf7387aaa2278a1.png)\n\nIdentify the points that **DO NOT** lie on the line $y=-2x$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-1,0)$, $B(-3,4)$, $C(0,0)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-1,0)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x \\\\ (0) &= -2(-1) \\\\ 0 &= 2 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-3,4)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x \\\\ (4) &= -2(-3) \\\\ 4 &= 6 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(0,0)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x \\\\ (0) &= -2(0) \\\\ 0 &= 0 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $B$ do not lie on the line.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "63ddadd2-69c2-522d-bef5-f2b951fb0a2a",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "35eee97b-8175-5fbd-a9cd-0ad6e49e272b",
