      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(2,-4)$, $B(3,-6)$, $C(-4,7)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(2,-4)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x \\\\ (-4) &= -2(2) \\\\ -4 &= -4 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(3,-6)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x \\\\ (-6) &= -2(3) \\\\ -6 &= -6 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(-4,7)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x \\\\ (7) &= -2(-4) \\\\ 7 &= 8 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $C$ does not lie on the line.",
