      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186054676/assets/4e97f20e3434a9b1422200daaefc12f38725b43030008357cd40823baaf4e2a7.png)\n\nIdentify the points that **DO NOT** lie on the line $y=-2x+3$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(3,-3)$, $B(-2,4)$, $C(1,1)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(3,-3)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+3 \\\\ (-3) &= -2(3)+3 \\\\ -3 &= -3 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-2,4)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+3 \\\\ (4) &= -2(-2)+3 \\\\ 4 &= 7 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(1,1)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+3 \\\\ (1) &= -2(1)+3 \\\\ 1 &= 1 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $B$ does not lie on the line.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "030610c9-dbd5-5ed3-8cc2-fdb93ec9af00",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "f0213b44-17ca-538b-9f4e-f6ba50029bf9",
