      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186054676/assets/6fe994f5a3d13bb618691b016b826e8f80fe9dfee7dedd56e59cdf3de1194b8b.png)\n\nIdentify the points that **DO NOT** lie on the line $y=-2x-2$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(2,-6)$, $B(-3,1)$, $C(0,-2)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(2,-6)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-2 \\\\ (-6) &= -2(2)-2 \\\\ -6 &= -6 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-3,1)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-2 \\\\ (1) &= -2(-3)-2 \\\\ 1 &= 4 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(0,-2)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-2 \\\\ (-2) &= -2(0)-2 \\\\ -2 &= -2 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $B$ does not lie on the line.",
