      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186054676/assets/0cd095b63d9032f626ef7f5093a212de49efe2cad1be7d2cfb7d7f7089724d91.png)\n\nIdentify the points that **DO NOT** lie on the line $y=-2x-1$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-2,4)$, $B(0,-2)$, $C(-3,5)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-2,4)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-1 \\\\ (4) &= -2(-2)-1 \\\\ 4 &= 3 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(0,-2)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-1 \\\\ (-2) &= -2(0)-1 \\\\ -2 &= -1 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(-3,5)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-1 \\\\ (5) &= -2(-3)-1 \\\\ 5 &= 5 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $B$ do not lie on the line.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "bfd7b305-56df-5bd1-b0a1-01595b1edee8",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "99f60ed2-b80b-5f7f-b120-7461b7b3c7fa",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$B$ and $C$ only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "eb1c70cc-124f-5e0e-94d1-27e646fae43f",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$A$ only"
