      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(2,-4)$, $B(0,4)$, $C(-2,6)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(2,-4)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -3x+2 \\\\ (-4) &= -3(2)+2 \\\\ -4 &= -4 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(0,4)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -3x+2 \\\\ (4) &= -3(0)+2 \\\\ 4 &= 2 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(-2,6)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -3x+2 \\\\ (6) &= -3(-2)+2 \\\\ 6 &= 8 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $B$ and $C$ do not lie on the line.",
