      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(3,-4)$, $B(0,3)$, $C(-3,8)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(3,-4)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+3 \\\\ (-4) &= -2(3)+3 \\\\ -4 &= -3 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(0,3)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+3 \\\\ (3) &= -2(0)+3 \\\\ 3 &= 3 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(-3,8)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+3 \\\\ (8) &= -2(-3)+3 \\\\ 8 &= 9 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $C$ do not lie on the line.",
