      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(2,-8)$, $B(-1,7)$, $C(0,-1)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(2,-8)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -5x+2 \\\\ (-8) &= -5(2)+2 \\\\ -8 &= -8 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-1,7)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -5x+2 \\\\ (7) &= -5(-1)+2 \\\\ 7 &= 7 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(0,-1)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -5x+2 \\\\ (-1) &= -5(0)+2 \\\\ -1 &= 2 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $C$ does not lie on the line.",
