      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186054676/assets/c2e37d3a645d21d9c33bdb5f50869c118d8c7bf2d6dd56e4d27113451d5fe229.png)\n\nIdentify the points that **DO NOT** lie on the line $y=-2x-1$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-3,5)$, $B(-4,4)$, $C(0,-1)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-3,5)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-1 \\\\ (5) &= -2(-3)-1 \\\\ 5 &= 5 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-4,4)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-1 \\\\ (4) &= -2(-4)-1 \\\\ 4 &= 7 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(0,-1)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-1 \\\\ (-1) &= -2(0)-1 \\\\ -1 &= -1 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $B$ does not lie on the line.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "ef128d61-e34d-57db-8fcf-a997aa6d3c08",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "b052ff79-4e97-512d-b19d-528ed29bbc46",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "$B$ and $C$ only"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "6582a2f6-9319-534f-92ad-3dbef1dc01df",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
