      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186054676/assets/9bd705bbd2648fb20494c717ea3ea3bb434123e543785f20c3b917255d5178c4.png)\n\nIdentify the points that **DO NOT** lie on the line $y=-4x-4$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-3,8)$, $B(-2,7)$, $C(0,-3)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-3,8)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -4x-4 \\\\ (8) &= -4(-3)-4 \\\\ 8 &= 8 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-2,7)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -4x-4 \\\\ (7) &= -4(-2)-4 \\\\ 7 &= 4 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(0,-3)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -4x-4 \\\\ (-3) &= -4(0)-4 \\\\ -3 &= -4 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $B$ and $C$ do not lie on the line.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
