      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(0,-3)$, $B(2,-7)$, $C(-2,3)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(0,-3)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -3x-3 \\\\ (-3) &= -3(0)-3 \\\\ -3 &= -3 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(2,-7)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -3x-3 \\\\ (-7) &= -3(2)-3 \\\\ -7 &= -9 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(-2,3)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -3x-3 \\\\ (3) &= -3(-2)-3 \\\\ 3 &= 3 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $B$ does not lie on the line.",
