      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186054676/assets/ddcfb5bbc80505157fb2dfdc015da61bbc8d7eadf65f543fece5ed84744b2272.png)\n\nIdentify the points that **DO NOT** lie on the line $y=-2x+4$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(1,-1)$, $B(3,-2)$, $C(0,7)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(1,-1)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+4 \\\\ (-1) &= -2(1)+4 \\\\ -1 &= 2 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(3,-2)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+4 \\\\ (-2) &= -2(3)+4 \\\\ -2 &= -2 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(0,7)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+4 \\\\ (7) &= -2(0)+4 \\\\ 7 &= 4 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $C$ do not lie on the line.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "d621662d-31dd-5ec8-bb4a-20bfee7178fa",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
