      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(0,4)$, $B(1,0)$, $C(3,-5)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(0,4)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+4 \\\\ (4) &= -2(0)+4 \\\\ 4 &= 4 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(1,0)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+4 \\\\ (0) &= -2(1)+4 \\\\ 0 &= 2 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(3,-5)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+4 \\\\ (-5) &= -2(3)+4 \\\\ -5 &= -2 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $B$ and $C$ do not lie on the line.",
